      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "**The Business of Strangers** (2001) represents a razor-sharp examination of corporate power dynamics through a feminist lens, with Stockard Channing delivering one of her most nuanced performances as Julie Styron, a hardened executive facing off against Julia Stiles' enigmatic young consultant. The film shares DNA with **Working Girl** (1988) and **9 to 5** (1980), but writer-director Patrick Stettner strips away the comedy to expose raw psychological warfare. Like **In the Company of Men** (1997), it uses the sterile hotel/corporate environment as a pressure cooker for exploring manipulation and revenge."
      },
