      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "What sets **The Business of Strangers** (2001) apart is its unflinching examination of mentorship gone wrong, sharing thematic DNA with **Black Swan** (2010) and **The Devil Wears Prada** (2006). The film subverts traditional corporate hierarchy narratives by presenting two women who recognize their own struggles in each other while simultaneously viewing the other as a threat. This complex dynamic elevates the film beyond simple workplace drama into a meditation on gender, power, and generational divide in corporate America."
